.TH AVR\-FIREWALL\-ADD 1 "" "avr" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-firewall-add \- Add a rule.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr firewall add
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add a rule.
.PP
Add a rule. Exactly one of --cidr, --fqdn, --any must be specified.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified.
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fITEXT\fR
Repository ID or owner/repo. If provided, adds at repo scope.
.TP
\fB\-\-action\fR \fICHOICE\fR
(choices: allow, deny; required)
.TP
\fB\-\-cidr\fR \fITEXT\fR
Destination CIDR (e.g. 10.0.0.0/8 or 1.2.3.4/32).
.TP
\fB\-\-fqdn\fR \fITEXT\fR
Destination hostname (e.g. api.example.com).
.TP
\fB\-\-any\fR
Set the catch-all default, preserving its ID if it already exists.
.TP
\fB\-\-proto\fR \fICHOICE\fR
(choices: tcp, udp, icmp, any; default: any)
.TP
\fB\-\-ports\fR \fITEXT\fR
Port or port range (0-65535), or all.
.TP
\fB\-\-position\fR \fIINTEGER\fR
Insert at a specific 0-indexed position.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-firewall (1),
